## Interface: 120100
## Title: Loot Advisor
## Notes: What dropped, how big an upgrade it is for everyone present, and what it would cost — at the moment the boss dies.
## Author: Gloom
## Version: @project-version@
## SavedVariables: HoDLootAdvisorDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: HoDLootAdvisorCharDB

# The CurseForge project the packager uploads to. Paired with the CF_API_TOKEN
# repo secret; remove either one and the CurseForge step is simply skipped while
# the GitHub Release still gets cut. See .github/workflows/release.yml for why
# CurseForge exists here at all (WoWUp's GitHub update path is broken).
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1671489

# Load order matters: the baked data table must exist before anything reads it,
# and Scoring must be on the namespace before Loot drives it.
LootData.lua
# Style.lua before anything that draws: it owns the fonts, the DS 2.0 palette and
# the surface primitives every window builds on. Pure data + helpers, no frames,
# so it is safe this early.
Style.lua
Scoring.lua
Core.lua
Settings.lua
Payload.lua
Diagnostics.lua
# Comms after Payload (it stores what it receives) and after Diagnostics (it
# logs what it cannot verify about itself). Everything it reads from the rest of
# the namespace is read at CALL time, so nothing below needs to precede it.
Comms.lua
# Roster after Comms: it asks Comms who is already reporting live, so it never
# inspects someone whose own client is telling us the same facts for free.
Roster.lua
Journal.lua
Targets.lua
Tooltip.lua
Record.lua
Loot.lua
LoadWindow.lua
RecordWindow.lua
Panel.lua
